WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.500
Good code is a start.
Pixelcraft. A coding-agent skill pack, not another UI template.

00:03.500 --> 00:07.500
Your agent. With a point of view.
Install the skills in your existing coding agent.

00:07.500 --> 00:10.000
One illustrative travel brief.
Explore genuinely different directions.

00:10.000 --> 00:12.500
Editorial. Electric. Sunlit.
Authored demonstration, not a live model response.

00:12.500 --> 00:15.000
Same brief. The familiar first draft.
The first answer is not the only answer.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.000
With Pixelcraft: hierarchy, rhythm, and character.
Build the whole experience, not just the first screen.

00:20.000 --> 00:22.500
Mobile. Native-minded, not web-shaped.
Clear priorities and reachable actions.

00:22.500 --> 00:25.000
Desktop. Dense, not difficult.
A workspace built for focus.

00:25.000 --> 00:28.000
Terminal. Even here, intent matters.
HTML and TUI emulations, not native applications.

00:28.000 --> 00:31.000
Freedom in the look. Rigor in the work.
Plan. Frame. Diverge. Specify.

00:31.000 --> 00:34.000
Build. Verify. Report.
Say what you actually checked.

00:34.000 --> 00:40.000
Make something unmistakably yours.
Pixelcraft. 26 skills. Open source. MIT licensed.
